
This folder contains isoconfigurational averages and model predictions of the KA model, separated into training and test set.

The ".tar.xz" file contains data in the numpy .npz format. 

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T0.44, T0.50, T0.56, T0.64:

The format of the files is: N4096T{TEMP}_{STRUCT}.npz where TEMP denotes the temperature and STRUCT denotes the index of the structure (1 - 500).

Each array contains the following information:

types: the type of each particle (1,2,3)
initial_positions: the initial positions of each particle in the structure
initial_positions_inherent: the initial positions in the inherent states of each particle in the structure
initial_positions_cage: the initial positions in the cage states of each particle in the structure (only for structures 1 - 100 (training) and 401 - 500 (test))
BOTAN: predictions of BOTAN (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
CAGE: predictions of CAGE (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
GlassMLP: predictions of GlassMLP (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
SE3: predictions of SE3 (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
SBO: Principal component of the smoothed bond-order parameters  (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
SBO_CG: Coarse-grained principal component of the smoothed bond-order parameters (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
DEN: Coarse-grained density (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
EPOT: Coarse-grained potential energy in the inherent states (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)
PSI6: Coarse-grained bond-order parameters Psi_6 (only for structures 401 - 500, only for type A particles)

example.py: Creates a snapshot of an exemplary configuration and colors each particle according to its propensity


